cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Consequence-Tiered API Governance for Autonomous AI Agents
message: If you use this specification, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dhanaraj
    given-names: Rinu
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # <-- replace with your ORCID
abstract: >-
  A runtime governance model for autonomous AI agents calling production APIs.
  Operations are classified by the consequence of incorrect execution across five
  criteria, declared in the OpenAPI specification at design time, and enforced at
  the API gateway at runtime. High-consequence operations are withheld at the
  gateway and authorised out-of-band, so that no human occupies the agent's
  synchronous request path.
keywords:
  - api-governance
  - ai-agents
  - agentic-ai
  - api-gateway
  - openapi
  - authorization
